Feature: Sales Data Processing in Unity Catalog

  Background: Initial Setup
    Given a Unity Catalog schema named "purgo_playground"
    And a dataset is available in a CSV format

  Scenario Outline: Validate Sales Data Entry
    Given the dataset is loaded into the "purgo_playground" schema
    When a record is processed with country code "<country_cd>", product ID "<product_id>", quantity sold "<qty_sold>", and sales date "<sales_date>"
    Then the record should be successfully validated if it meets the criteria

    Examples:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15 |
      | US         | P1002      | 30       | 2024-01-16 |
      | CA         | P1001      | 40       | 2024-01-15 |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17 |
      | UK         | P1002      | 35       | 2024-01-18 |
      | UK         | P1004      | 20       | 2024-01-19 |
      | IN         | P1001      | 60       | 2024-01-20 |
      | IN         | P1003      | 45       | 2024-01-21 |
      | AU         | P1004      | 55       | 2024-01-22 |
      | AU         | P1002      | 38       | 2024-01-23 |

  Scenario: Validate Country Code Format
    Given the dataset is loaded into the "purgo_playground" schema
    When a record is processed
    Then the field "country_cd" must be a valid ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code

  Scenario: Validate Non-Negative Quantity Sold
    Given the dataset is loaded into the "purgo_playground" schema
    When a record is processed
    Then the field "qty_sold" must be a non-negative integer

  Scenario: Validate Product ID Format
    Given the dataset is loaded into the "purgo_playground" schema
    When a record is processed
    Then the field "product_id" must match the pattern "P\d{4}"

  Scenario: Validate Sales Date Format
    Given the dataset is loaded into the "purgo_playground" schema
    When a record is processed
    Then the field "sales_date" must be in "YYYY-MM-DD" format

  Scenario: Handle Missing Data Entries
    Given the dataset has been checked for completeness
    When a record is missing any data entries
    Then an error message "Missing data in one or more fields" should be generated

  Scenario: Duplicate Entry Error
    Given the dataset is loaded into the "purgo_playground" schema
    When a duplicate entry is processed
    Then an error message "Duplicate entry detected" should be generated

  Scenario Outline: Successful Data Processing
    Given the record is valid
    When processed in the schema "purgo_playground"
    Then the record is stored successfully

    Examples:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15 |
      | IN         | P1003      | 45       | 2024-01-21 |
  
  Scenario: Invalid Sales Date
    Given the dataset is loaded into the "purgo_playground" schema
    When the "sales_date" is not in a valid format
    Then an error message "Invalid sales date format" should be generated